  "task_id": "tmm_design_a_26_layer_planar_dielectric_stack_on_fus_717566c523",
  "user_request_original": "Design a 26-layer planar dielectric stack on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Layer sequence: alternating HfO2 (high index) and SiO2 (low index), starting with HfO2 at air interface, ending with SiO2 at substrate (13 H-L pairs total). Initialize thicknesses using quadratic chirp profile with base period centered at 375 nm for UV reflection band, then apply gradient-based thickness optimization. Enforce hard bounds: all layer thicknesses must be clamped to [20 nm, 250 nm] immediately after initialization and maintained throughout optimization. Evaluate at normal incidence, unpolarized light. Spectral bands: maximize reflectance in 300-450 nm, maximize transmittance in 1000-1700 nm. Use coherent TMM. Report thicknesses_nm, best_target_score, valid_candidates, tightest_margin, run_status. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 300-450 nm, 1000-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmission in 1000-1700 nm; high reflection in 300-450 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: reflection in 1000-1700 nm; transmission in 300-450 nm. manufacturing constraints: Maximum total layer count of 30.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Design a 26-layer HfO2/SiO2 planar stack on fused silica under air incidence, initialized with a 375 nm-centered quadratic chirp profile and clamped to [20, 250] nm. Optimize layer thicknesses via gradient-based search at normal incidence to maximize reflectance in 300–450 nm and transmittance in 1000–1700 nm while suppressing reflection in the IR band and transmission in the UV band.",
